@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
title Behavior - Reorder siblings
actor "Authorized user" as actor
box "Frontend - Mission Control application" #E0F2FE
  participant "WorkHierarchyBranch, or MovePositionDialog / MovePositionForm" as page
  participant "IWorkOrderService / WorkOrderService" as client
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Api" #D1FADF
  participant "CurrentAccountAuthorization" as access
  participant "WorkOrdersController" as ctrl
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "ValidationBehavior" as validation
  participant "ReorderSiblingCommandHandler" as handler
  participant "WorkOrder" as entity
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  database "Mission Control SQL" as db
end box
actor -> page : Move up / Move down on an outline row (row menu below 768px), or Move to position... from the outline or the detail page
page -> page : Move up / Move down: WorkHierarchyBranch snapshots its saved sibling order and shows the item at its new place as Saving. Move to position: the page opens MovePositionDialog with a MoveTarget (position, count, order version from the read that drew the row; nothing read on open). One move at a time, never debounced
opt Cancel, Close, or Escape after choosing another position in the dialog
  page -> page : The chosen position is a dirty draft: UnsavedChangesDialog asks first; Discard closes and sends nothing
end
page -> client : reorderSibling(ReorderSiblingCommand: parent, item, absolute target position, expected sibling-order version: WorkItemPage.orderVersion of the branch, or WorkItemDetail.siblingOrderVersion)
client -> access : PUT /api/workspaces/{id}/work-order/siblings
access -> access : L2-002 validate signature, issuer, audience, subject, expiry
access -> db : Read current status, role and credential version
db --> access : Current account access
alt Missing, invalid or expired JWT; deactivated account
  access --> client : 401; audit denial without payloads
  client --> page : sessionInterceptor calls SessionService.end(Unauthorized) once for this generation; the promise rejects with its 401 (nothing written); restore snapshot; sign-in shows session-unsaved when a draft was dirty, then returns to the outline
else Authenticated active account (profile P: reordering needs no capability beyond an active session)
  access -> ctrl : Authorized request
  ctrl -> validation : Send ReorderSiblingCommand through MediatR 12.5.0
  validation -> validation : Identifiers well formed; target position is a whole number of 1 or more
  alt Malformed request
    validation --> ctrl : 400 field errors; nothing read or changed
    ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails
    client --> page : Restore snapshot; MovePositionDialog keeps the value and focus moves to the position field, which reads its message; no Retry or reference ID
  else Valid request
    validation -> handler : Handle ReorderSiblingCommand
    handler -> db : BeginWorkspaceTransactionAsync takes the workspace lock first; LoadSiblingOrderAsync loads the tracked sibling order under the parent and its order version
    db --> handler : Ordered stable IDs and version, or lock-wait timeout
    alt Workspace lock wait times out
      handler --> ctrl : 503 with Retry-After; nothing read or changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (unavailable)
      client --> page : Unavailable save: restore snapshot; keep focus on the move control; Try again resends the same move only when chosen (move-failed on the outline, failed in the dialog)
    else Workspace, parent, or item not found
      handler --> ctrl : 404; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (not found)
      client --> page : The branch rereads without the item and announces that it no longer exists; with no dialog open the focused row is gone, so focus moves to the branch's parent row, or to the Work heading for an initiative; an open dialog closes with NotFound, and the page increments its refresh counter and shows the toast
    else Item not a sibling under that parent, other workspace, or position beyond the sibling count (L2-017.3)
      handler --> ctrl : 400 invalid position or reference; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails
      client --> page : Restore snapshot; the dialog shows "Enter a position from 1 to N" with focus on the position field (out-of-range state); an inline move shows the reason with Reload order, without Try again or a reference ID
    else Stale sibling-order version (L2-041)
      handler --> ctrl : 409 order changed; nothing applied
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (order changed)
      client --> page : Restore snapshot; never resent. Outline: "The order changed" alert announced without moving focus, because the move controls stay enabled; Reload order only, which rereads the loaded window and returns focus to the item's row (move-failed conflict variant). Dialog: Move gives way to Reload order, which receives focus and closes the dialog with Outdated (conflict state)
    else Move permitted
      handler -> entity : L2-017 move within the sibling set
      entity --> handler : Deterministic affected interval; every sibling present once
      handler -> db : L2-039 / L2-040 AddAuditEvent, then SaveChangesAsync: rewrite the affected interval, bump the sibling-order version, and record success audit in one transaction; release the lock
      alt Commit fails
        db --> handler : Roll back business state and success audit
        handler --> ctrl : Generic 500 with correlation ID
        ctrl --> client : Failure; no successful-move claim
        client --> page : Restore snapshot; alert with reference ID; keep focus on the move control; Try again resends the same move (move-failed on the outline, failed in the dialog)
      else Commit succeeds
        db --> handler : New sibling-order version
        handler --> ctrl : Committed order
        ctrl --> client : 200 OrderMoved (position, total, order version)
        client --> page : WorkHierarchyBranch rereads its loaded sibling window; after Move to position the dialog closes with Moved and the opening page increments its refresh counter (the outline rereads its expanded branches; the detail rereads its sibling position)
        page --> actor : Announce "{title} moved to position N of M" (the "Reordered" toast after the dialog); focus stays on the moved item's control, which stays focusable with aria-disabled at either end of the order
      end
    end
  end
end
opt No response to the move (timeout or network failure)
  client --> page : The move may have committed. Move up or Move down: the branch rereads its loaded window and the move-failed alert says "We couldn't confirm whether {title} moved" and where the reread found it, without a reference ID or Try again. Dialog: the failed alert with that title and no reference ID; the form emits unconfirmed, so the page rereads at once; Try again resends only when pressed, and a 409 to that resend drops "Nothing was applied" and says to reload to see where the item is now
end
note over ctrl, db
An unexpected 403 applies nothing; WorkHierarchyBranch restores its snapshot (or MovePositionForm keeps the position) and emits forbidden, and the routed page shows the "Your access changed" toast through TOAST_SERVICE, without Retry or reference ID; the capability refresh still runs.
All rejection checks run under the lock before any write; a stale version in SaveChangesAsync raises ConcurrencyConflictException, the same 409.
Unexpected failures return generic 500 plus correlation ID (L2-043).
Diagnostics exclude secrets and contact payloads.
end note
@enduml
